WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.025
Check yourself with two questions.

2
00:00:02.025 --> 00:00:04.938
First: you set role
settings at a subscription.

3
00:00:04.938 --> 00:00:06.838
Does a resource group under it get them?

4
00:00:06.838 --> 00:00:08.675
The answer is b: no.

5
00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:11.871
Microsoft Learn says the
settings aren't inherited,

6
00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:14.250
so the file lists every governed scope.

7
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:19.075
Second: a deployment pipeline's service
principal holds standing Contributor.

8
00:00:19.075 --> 00:00:20.337
What does the plan do?

9
00:00:20.337 --> 00:00:24.110
The answer is c: it reports A
Z oh two and leaves it alone,

10
00:00:24.110 --> 00:00:27.712
because service principals
can't be made eligible.

11
00:00:27.712 --> 00:00:30.000
You saw it in Lab 1, step four.

12
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:34.970
The module page has two more questions,
each linked to the section that answers it.
